+# M10.5 · Free persistence of one material load
+
+## Requested decision
+
+Assess the bounded, gateway-prepared one-load excitation for OpenWave row 4. The home observer records which of twelve ports holds the load after free evolution. This would replace the nominated M10.4 two-load object and its thirty-seam reader for this row. M10.4 remains the accepted historical result. [Row criterion](https://github.com/openwave-labs/openwave/blob/bab6818b4a278ffef083c1e86c12134e5ff14ab5/MODELS.md#L104) · [Prior decision](https://github.com/openwave-labs/openwave/pull/749#pullrequestreview-6060088147)
+
+## Frozen settings
+
+Use the 20-cell Interval Echo board, all collars blank, one sharp loaded port, and the original native seam and degree terms. During acquisition address the thirty internal seams for one unit, then query the three gateways for occupancy by signed echo and undo. After 1,024 clear rounds open all seams. A click routes the same sharp load by native swaps to the next port. Cycle through twelve addresses in the appointed direction up to four times. Each fresh flight ends at one terminal read. The twelve internal ports, accepted exterior and exhausted source exhaust the outcomes. Scheduled exposures use exchange units. The excitation has no assigned species.
+
+For each of the four arms report all fourteen probabilities. Use coherent native flight, a port measurement at release followed by native flight, a uniform sharp baseline, and classical Poisson swaps at rate one half on each seam from the accepted source. Require a certified unconditional all-time home floor and a coherent terminal return each strictly above 0.94. Require the random-swap home probability below 0.80 and a coherent advantage over dephasing of at least 0.05. Require normalization within 2e-10 and agreement with an independent raw-edge reconstruction to 1e-9 in every bin. Retain rejected and incomplete results.
